course: dictionary
lesson: 684
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter. Balmoral is a name, so it is a proper noun. «Queen Elizabeth II died on 8 September 2022 at Balmoral in Scotland, aged 96.» The words Queen and Scotland are clues that Balmoral is a place.
explain: Balmoral Castle is a large castle in the Highlands of Scotland, and it is a private holiday home of the British royal family. When you read «at Balmoral» in news about the royals, the words around it tell you it means the castle, not a cap.
explain: Always check the words around the name. If the story is about the royals or Scotland, Balmoral means the place. If the story is about clothes, a balmoral is a flat Scottish cap, or a kind of laced boot, and it has no capital letter in that sense.
fact: A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Balmoral» can mean Balmoral Castle, a large castle in the Highlands of Scotland.
fact: Balmoral Castle is a private holiday home of the British royal family.
fact: The royal family often spend late summer at Balmoral.
fact: «A balmoral» can also mean a flat Scottish cap, or a kind of laced boot.
exercise: «Queen Elizabeth II died on 8 September 2022 at Balmoral in Scotland, aged 96.» What is Balmoral in this sentence? | A city in Wales | A kind of cheese | *A large castle in Scotland, a royal holiday home | A flat Scottish cap worn with a suit
exercise: Ella reads about «a balmoral» in a story about old Scottish clothes. What does it mean? | *A flat Scottish cap, or a kind of laced boot | A large castle in the Highlands | A royal holiday home | A type of Scottish bread
exercise: Why does Balmoral start with a capital letter? | It is a long word | *It is the name of one special place | It is the first word of a sentence in every case | It is always printed in bold
test: «Balmoral Castle is a large castle in the Highlands of Scotland.» What kind of word is Balmoral here? | A verb, an action word | An adjective, a describing word | A pronoun, a word like he or it | *A proper noun, the name of one place
test: A story about tartan and tweed says, «He wore a balmoral on his head.» What does balmoral mean here? | A large castle in the Highlands | *A flat Scottish cap | A mountain in Scotland | A member of the royal family
exam: Read «Queen Elizabeth II died on 8 September 2022 at Balmoral in Scotland, aged 96.» What does Balmoral mean here, and how do you know? | *A royal castle in Scotland, because the words Queen and Scotland give the clue | A word meaning sad, because the Queen died | A cap worn on the head, because it is a clothing word | A kind of boat, because it is near the water
